{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for the deployment note at exact clean head 32886357c038bed3cf290fb232fce58ff7e5d0dc. Independent checks: git diff --check, make vet, and make test pass; the worktree was clean before and after. The three prior findings improved materially. Atomic claim acquisition is now structurally correct: official git-push semantics make --atomic itself request the advertised capability and fail without updating refs if the receiver lacks it, so the real claim command plus a no-fallback nonzero-exit refusal is sufficient capability detection; case 10 can prove that. repository_dispatch is correctly removed. Fixed-width digest refs close the path-length defect. Four issues remain. F1 BLOCKER: the digest input is only called an unambiguous encoding; no encoding is defined. Concatenation is ambiguous, delimiter schemes fail on arbitrary keys, and text normalization/byte encoding can diverge across submitter and drain. Specify one byte-exact construction such as canonical CBOR array or length-prefixed UTF-8 fields, including normalization policy, and make case 9 compare adversarial boundary-shift tuples plus independent producer/drain implementations. Without that, recomputation does not bind the four-part identity. F2 MUST FIX: schedule-only invalidates the stated latency of seconds to a minute. GitHub documents a shortest schedule interval of five minutes, possible high-load delay and dropped queued jobs, default-branch-only execution, and public-repository auto-disable after 60 inactive days. State the actual 0-to-5-minute-plus-unbounded-delay posture and the monitoring/reactivation condition appropriate to the control repository. F3 MUST FIX: case 2 can now pass without exercising its named subject. Inbox pushes no longer trigger runs, so N pushes followed by one scheduled run trivially yields at most N runs and N admissions; that proves backlog draining, not concurrency-group coalescing. Rename it to backlog drain, or deliberately overlap scheduled/manual trusted runs and prove pending-run replacement while the survivor drains all work. F4 BLOCKER: case 6 promises the next Action run will re-push the true pre-vandalism head, but the stated hosted Action runner is ephemeral and the submission repository ref is the vandalized value. No durable trusted replica or remembered frontier is named, so a fresh run cannot distinguish a valid rewind from the true frontier or recover missing commits. Name a control-plane mirror/witness/ref and its update/recovery protocol, or change the case and posture to manual key-holder/auditor recovery. What held: cases 1, 3-5, 7-10 otherwise exercise their subjects with observable failures; atomic claim plus explicit leases preserves inbox on conflict; digest width and real ref creation close the original length gap; schedule-only restores control-repo authority isolation.","body":{"commit":"32886357c038bed3cf290fb232fce58ff7e5d0dc","head":"32886357c038bed3cf290fb232fce58ff7e5d0dc","verdict":"changes-requested"}}